course: dictionary
lesson: 8633
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them as numbered meanings, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Blue-green scum on a lake can be poisonous algae, so do not swim and keep dogs out.» Here scum is a dirty layer on top of the water, not a person.
explain: The first meaning is a dirty layer that forms on top of a liquid, like on a pond or bath water. «In hard-water areas, minerals in the water react with soap to make grey scum» shows how scum can form when soap is used in water.
explain: The second meaning is an insulting word for people thought to be very bad. It is a rude, hurtful word, so never use it to call anyone names. When you read scum, ask: is the writer talking about a liquid, or about people? The words around it give you the answer.
fact: Scum means a dirty layer that forms on top of a liquid.
fact: Pond scum is a dirty, slimy layer that can float on a pond.
fact: Soap scum forms when soap reacts with minerals in hard water.
fact: Skim off the scum means to scoop the layer off the top of a liquid.
fact: Calling a person scum is a very rude insult, so it is never a kind word to use.
exercise: «Blue-green scum on a lake can be poisonous algae.» Where is the scum? | On a hill | Inside a cake | In a school bag | *On the top of the water
exercise: Mum says the bath has a grey ring and calls it soap scum. What is soap scum? | *A dirty layer that forms on water when soap is used | A spoon for stirring | A type of sweet made with soap | A loud noise in the bathroom
exercise: Jay calls his brother «scum» to be mean. What does scum mean when it is used about people? | Very clean and tidy | A type of fish | *An insulting word for people thought to be very bad | A kind name for a good friend
test: «In hard-water areas, minerals in the water react with soap to make grey scum.» What is the grey scum? | A fizzy drink | A happy face drawn on a bath | *A layer that forms on the water when soap reacts with minerals | A soft toy
test: Which sentence uses scum to mean people? | The pond had green scum floating on it | The bath was covered in grey scum | The kettle had white scum in it | *He called the thief scum, which is a rude insult
exam: Pupil reads «skim off the scum» in a science book. What should they do? | Swim in the pond | Eat the scum with a spoon | Call a friend scum | *Scoop the layer off the top with a spoon
